  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-110" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="text-align:center"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;NEXTERA ENERGY TRANSMISSION SOUTHWEST, LLC. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:center"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;NOTES TO FINANCIAL STATEMENTS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:center"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;FOR THE NINE MONTHS ENDED SEPTEMBER 30, 2026 and 2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:center"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;(in thousands, unless otherwise noted)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:center"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Introduction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The accompanying financial statements were prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission ("FERC") as set forth in its applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting that varies from generally accepted accounting principles in the United States of America ("GAAP"). These requirements differ from GAAP related to (1) the presentation of deferred income taxes, (2) the presentation of regulatory debits and credits, (3) the presentation of regulatory assets and liabilities, (4) treatment of equity carrying charges, and (5) the presentation of accruals associated with the cost of removal included within the accumulated depreciation reserve. Accordingly, certain footnotes are not prepared on the same basis as the financial statements presented herein.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;NextEra Energy Transmission&#8239;Southwest,&#8239;LLC&#8239;(NEET Southwest) is&#8239;a&#8239;subsidiary&#8239;of NextEra Energy Transmission, LLC (NEET), a leading competitive transmission company in North America, is focused on developing transmission assets in the&#8239;Southwest Power Pool (SPP)&#8239;region.&#8239;&#8239; On April&#8239;26, 2022,&#8239;NEET&#8239;Southwest&#8239;was awarded the Minco-Pleasant Valley-Draper (Minco) project by the SPP to construct a new&#8239;approximately&#8239;48&#8239;miles of 345 kV transmission facilities in Oklahoma, interconnecting the Minco substation in Grady County and the Pleasant Valley and Draper substations in Cleveland County. Minco commenced commercial operations on January 30, 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;In addition to Minco, NEET Southwest is developing the following transmission projects: On October&#8239;27, 2021, NEET&#8239;Southwest&#8239;was awarded&#8239;the Wolf Creek-Blackberry transmission project by SPP. The project is approximately 94 miles of 345 kV transmission line that will run from the Wolf Creek substation in Coffey County, Kansas to the Blackberry substation in Jasper County, Missouri. Wolf Creek-Blackberry commenced commercial operations on July 15, 2025. In August 2023, NEET Southwest was awarded the Crossroads &#8211; Hobbs &#8211; Roadrunner project by the SPP to construct a new approximately 135 miles of 345 kV transmission line in New Mexico. The Crossroads-Hobbs-Roadrunner project went into service in April 2026. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;___________________________________________________________________________&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
  <ferc:ReportYear id="f-111" contextRef="c-1" decimals="0" unitRef="u-1">2026</ferc:ReportYear>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantContingentAssetsOrLiabilitiesTextBlock id="f-112" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;1. &#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;REGULATORY MATTERS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Challenge to New Mexico Renewable Transmission Authority&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;In November 2023, Southwestern Public Service Company (&#8220;SPS&#8221;) submitted a challenge to the New Mexico Renewable Energy Transmission Authority&#8217;s (&#8220;NM RETA&#8221;) decision to work with NEET Southwest on the Crossroads-Hobbs-Roadrunner project. On March 27, 2024, NM RETA issued a final decision rejecting SPS&#8217;s challenge.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;On April 25, 2024, SPS appealed NM RETA&#8217;s decision to the New Mexico District Court for the First District. Oral argument was held on January 31, 2025, and the District Court issued a decision on April 10, 2025, affirming NM RETA&#8217;s decision and rejecting SPS&#8217;s challenges. SPS has 30 days from the date of the District Court order to further appeal to the New Mexico Court of Appeals. On May 12, 2025, SPS filed a request to the New Mexico Court of Appeals for an extension of its May 12 deadline to file an appeal, which the Court of Appeals granted. SPS filed its writ petition on May 29, 2025, and NEET Southwest and NM RETA responded in opposition on June 13, 2025. On June 30, 2025, the New Mexico Court of Appeals granted SPS&#8217;s writ petition. SPS requested a 6-month extension of time to submit its brief, in order to allow for settlement discussions with RETA, which the New Mexico Court of Appeals granted on October. 21, 2025. SPS and NMRETA filed a settlement to resolve the matter, which NEET Southwest did not oppose, and the case has been dismissed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantContingentAssetsOrLiabilitiesTextBlock>
  <ferc:RespondentLegalName id="f-113" contextRef="c-1">NextEra Energy Transmission Southwest, LLC.</ferc:RespondentLegalName>
  <ferc:ReportDate id="f-114" contextRef="c-1">2026-11-04</ferc:ReportDate>
  <ferc:ReportYear id="f-115" contextRef="c-1" decimals="0" unitRef="u-1">2026</ferc:ReportYear>
  <ferc:ReportPeriod id="f-116" contextRef="c-1">Q3</ferc:ReportPeriod>
